# Scenario 'forced_dead' (FORCED execution, published under traces/forced/, never part of the natural union): code behind `ret` patches and unreferenced routines, entered with the
# harness directive `force BB:AAAA [A=..] [HL=..]` (docs/research/dynamic_tracing.md, section 11) from the logo screen after a power cycle. What each call is (symbol notes):
#   23:58C5 / 23:5FA3 / 23:669A   bodies of the three disabled sprite counters (SpriteCounter_StubA/B/C start with `ret`): digits of HL as sprites
#   22:48CD / 23:47BC             dead twin routines that print wRam_C2D7/C2D6/C2D5 as decimal numbers (a time read-out)
#   2C:741C                       unused address-book screen "みる < START > かく" with a yes/no dialog (message id $0204)
#   2B:6CF5                       unreachable twin of Mailbox_ReplyToRecord
#   67:424A                       unreferenced "phone number changed" flag helper (compares SRAM 1:B08B/B09C with DEDD/DEEE)
#   29:5117-29:5335               the HYPOTHESIS palette-fade library (wait for LY=$90, fades) entered at each function start
# Arguments not stated are zero. Starts from the state left by 'tutorial_profile'. Screen names = my reading of the screenshots.
